From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Casper Yang <casperyang2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:04:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Close Brk's pages the way Chrome closes a tab

Brk deleted a page's WebContents directly, so its beforeunload, pagehide and unload handlers never ran: Discord, which keeps
its session token out of localStorage while it thinks DevTools are open and writes it back from beforeunload, signed the user
out every time its pinned tab's page was closed (issue #11). -close now goes through TabStripModel::CloseWebContentsAt, as
Chrome's tab close does, with a 2 s limit after which the page is deleted anyway. -confirmLeaving: runs beforeunload alone, so
the shell can ask Leave this page? before it lets a page go; a hook in BrowserWebContentsDelegate::BeforeUnloadFired keeps
that answer from going on to unload, and the close that follows runs only the unload handlers.
---
 brk/browser/brk_application.mm                |   2 +
 brk/browser/brk_browser.h                     |   3 +
 brk/browser/brk_browser.mm                    |  11 ++
 brk/browser/brk_web_contents.h                |   2 +
 brk/browser/brk_web_contents.mm               | 111 +++++++++++++++++-
 brk/embedding/embedding.h                     |   3 +
 .../browser_web_contents_delegate.cc          |   1 +
 7 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

